sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Q as Ola (requester, sector 112)
  participant M as Mesh (routers + phones, 10-hop radius)
  participant K as Marek (nearest capable citizen to the AED)
  participant O as Other responders in range
  participant G as Gateway / Authority
  Q->>M: LIFE_CRITICAL "cardiac arrest, AED needed" (signed, top priority)
  M->>M: flood with de-duplication, pre-empt all other classes
  M->>K: request + registered AED record 40 m from Marek, Ola 200 m further
  M->>O: same request, lower rank (farther from the AED)
  K->>M: signed acceptance "fetching AED"
  M->>Q: acceptance back along path, ETA shown to Ola
  M->>O: request marked taken; CPR-trained neighbour still asked to go to Ola
  M->>K: guidance: to the AED, then to Ola (hop distance, direction)
  K-->>Q: Marek runs the AED over in about 90 s (staff would take 6 min)
  Q->>M: CLOSE signed by requester, responders notified
  M->>G: event reaches a gateway when a path exists, dashboard updated
  Note over Q,G: Messages travel hop by hop. The object travels with one person.
